This small print pictures the O-Torii (Grand Torii Gate) at Itsukushima Shrine on the island of Itsukushima (popularly known as Miyajima.) O-Torii was designated as a National Important Cultural Property on March 29, 1952.&lt;br&gt;
This print carries a seal reading 紫園 &quot;Shien&quot; which is believed to have been created by the publisher Watanabe Shōzaburō as a &quot;house&quot; seal for use on postcard size prints. Both Kawase Hasui 川瀬巴水 (1883-1957) and Kasamatsu Shirō 笠松紫浪 (1898–1991) are thought to possibly be the designers of these prints marked &quot;Shien.&quot;
