A beautiful small (postcard size) print picturing a ferryboat on its way to, or passing by, Kankaikaku (Kankai Pavilion or, literally, sea viewing pavilion) which sits across from the Kimii-dera temple complex and its Tahōtō (two-story pagoda) in Wakanoura a scenic area in the southwestern part of Wakayama Prefecture .
