A postcard-size print picturing Kyoto&#39;s Kiyomizu Temple in snow. Kiyomizu was one of the most frequently portrayed temples in Japanese prints. The publisher of this print was Yokohama-based Hideo Takemura (H. Takemura &amp; Co.) who targeted his work at a Western audience, specializing in, as printed on his business card, Christmas Cards, Japanese Old Colour Prints, Famous Modern Colour Prints and Water Colors. 
