An undated (c. 1930s) small format reproduction loosely based on Hiroshige&#39;s The Monkey Bridge in Kai Province, originally issued between 1840 and 1842 and designed as part of a four panel harimaze print.  The bridge got its name because the original rickety, plank structure was so precarious that only an agile monkey could supposedly cross it. 
