Nan&#39;endō, located at the southwest edge of Nara Park, is the ninth temple along the Saigoku Kannon Pilgrimage. Nakazawa shows us couples strolling along Sarusawa Pond while the famous Nara Park deer tend to their business. In the background we see the octagonal Nan&#39;endō Hall on the right and the pagoda, left-center, is likely the three-story Sanjū-no-tō. Nan&#39;endō is within the Kōfuku-ji 興福寺 complex.&lt;br&gt;
