Nakazawa focuses on the Wollastonite rock formations (formed when limestone are subjected to high temperature such as magma) upon which the temple is built and which gave the temple its name, Ishiyama-dera (Rock Mountain Temple). It is the thirteenth temple along the Saigoku Kannon Pilgrimage.&lt;br&gt;
