Picturing the puppet Omitsu in the play The New Scandalous Ballad of Osome and Hisamatsu written by Chikamatsu Hanji (1725-1783) and first staged in 1780.&lt;br&gt;

A story of unrequited love and double suicide.  In Nozaki Mura the country girl Omitsu is in love with Hisamatsu, but he is in love with the city girl Osome. Aware that they might commit double suicide if thwarted, Omitsu cuts her hair off to become a nun.&lt;br&gt;

