An illustration of the stage set for Act VII “The Teahouse in Gion” of the play Kanadehon Chūshingura [The Treasury of Loyal Retainers] attributed to the playwrights Takeda Izumo II (1691-1756), Miyoshi Shōraku (1696-1772) and Namiki Senryū (1695-1751) and first performed in 1748.&lt;br&gt;

This set presents us with the teahouse and its veranda where Yuranosuke, Okaru and Heiemon will come together in a passionate scene in which Heiemon begs to take his sister Okaru&#39;s life before Yuranosuke intervenes to allow Okaru to live and Heiemon to enter the league of the loyal retainers. Yuranosuke has been feigning a life of debauchery at the teahouse as part of his plan to avenge his former lord. &lt;br&gt;

