Perhaps depicting an Edo period personal injury lawsuit. The injured man claims, &quot;I fell off the palanquin because of the improper pace of the palanquin carriers, I will report this insolence to the bakufu.&quot; He then reaches a settlement with the people of the post station and the palanquin carriers. However, the text accompanying the image is unread.
&lt;br&gt;The signature to the right of the text appears to read かのめ 明行 (Kanome? Aiyuki?), but the transcription and reading of the characters is not confirmed. This may be the signature of the writer of the inscription. The artist who drew the image is unknown.
